                    'en' => [
                        'name' => 'Ammar ibn Yasir',
                        'full_name' => 'Ammar ibn Yasir ibn Amir al-Ansi, ally of Banu Makhzum',
                        'kunya' => 'Abul-Yaqzan',
                        'laqab' => 'At-Tayyib al-Mutayyab (the Pure and Purified), Son of Sumayyah',
                        'biography' => "Ammar ibn Yasir was among the first believers tortured for Allah's sake, the son of the first two martyrs of Islam. His father Yasir, a Yemeni of the Ans tribe, settled in Mecca as an ally of Banu Makhzum and married their bondwoman Sumayyah; Ammar was their son. The family embraced Islam at the very beginning, at the house of al-Arqam, and Banu Makhzum tortured them on the burning sands of Mecca. The Prophet ﷺ would pass by them and say: 'Patience, family of Yasir — your appointed place is Paradise.' Yasir died under torture, and Abu Jahl speared Sumayyah, making her the first martyr of Islam. Ammar himself was coerced until he uttered words against the Prophet while his heart rested firm in faith — and the verse came down: 'Except one who is compelled while his heart is secure in faith' (16:106). He migrated to Medina, fought at Badr, Uhud, the Trench and every campaign, and was the first man to build a mosque in Islam, gathering stones for the mosque of Quba. The Prophet said: 'Ammar is filled with faith to the marrow of his bones,' and prophesied: 'Ammar will be killed by the transgressing party.' Umar appointed him governor of Kufa, calling him one of the nobles. In the civil strife he stood with Ali at the Camel and Siffin, a man of ninety-three chanting: 'Today I meet the beloved ones — Muhammad and his band!' He fell at Siffin in Safar 37 AH, and his death revealed to all the truth of the Prophet's prophecy.",
                        'virtues' => "Among the first believers; son of Islam's first two martyrs. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Patience, family of Yasir — your appointed place is Paradise,' and 'Ammar is filled with faith to the marrow.' Quranic revelation confirmed his steadfastness under torture, and he built the first mosque in Islam.",
                        'famous_narrations' => "He narrated 62 hadiths; the most famous report concerning him is the Prophet's prophecy: 'Ammar will be killed by the transgressing party — he calls them to Paradise and they call him to the Fire.'",
                        'martyrdom' => "Ammar was martyred at Siffin in Safar 37 AH at the age of ninety-three, fighting in Ali's ranks while chanting: 'Today I meet the beloved ones — Muhammad and his band!' He drank a draught of milk, recalling the Prophet's words that his last drink in this world would be milk, then advanced and was slain — fulfilling the prophecy 'the transgressing party will kill him.' He was buried at Siffin.",
